  <div class="lg:col-span-9 grid gap-14 lg:gap-20">
    <section id="a" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="a-h">
      <h2 id="a-h" class="h2">Before you get in touch.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="a1">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What should I send in the first message?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A short, neutral message through WhatsApp or Signal, such as: "I'd like a private conversation. Please let me know the next step." Dr. Tabansky replies personally as soon as possible. Do not send passwords, recovery codes, screenshots, legal documents, intimate material or details, or detailed allegations in that first message. Keep identifying case details out of it as well.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="a2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can someone notice my contact with Toza?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Contact through WhatsApp or Signal is not guaranteed to be invisible on your device or account. Keep the first message short and neutral.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="a3" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Is the first conversation the paid service?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. The first conversation checks whether Toza fits your situation, whether anything appears urgent and what the next step should be. It is free and includes no device inspection, mapping, diagnosis or technical work. Contacting Toza does not commit you to a purchase.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="a4" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What happens before I pay?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>If the service fits, you receive a written offer with the work, inclusions, exclusions, price, agreed additions and payment terms. You accept it explicitly and pay; then the visit is scheduled. No paid work starts before acceptance and receipt of payment. Preparation instructions are sent directly.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="a5">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Do I need to know what's wrong before I get in touch?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. You can have a concern, a hunch, or a wish to take a more deliberate approach to your digital life. You do not need to identify an account, setting or technical fault. The first conversation checks whether Toza fits; examining your digital environment belongs to the first step. A concern alone does not establish that someone has accessed your information.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="b" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="b-h">
      <h2 id="b-h" class="h2">The first step ({{ facts.prices.assessment | ils }}).</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="b1" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What do I get for {{ facts.prices.assessment | ils }}?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A senior check-up of your digital life: half a day in person with Dr. Tabansky. He listens to your concerns, inspects the relevant devices, accounts and access, and explains what the findings mean for you. Where urgent exposure can be addressed safely within the agreed scope, he makes the changes with your approval. You keep a written exposure summary with ordered next steps. The {{ facts.prices.assessment | ils }} counts in full toward a tier that begins within {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="b2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What does it cover, and how long does it take?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>{{ facts.assessmentScope | capfirst }}. Dr. Tabansky reviews the relevant identities, accounts, apps, permissions, signed-in devices, recovery routes and shared services. Allow half a day; it typically takes four hours. The visit completes the agreed intake, access mapping, diagnosis and approved urgent first aid. The review stays within your authorized environment and is not a promise to find accounts or devices that have not been identified.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="b3" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What do I receive if I don't continue?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A written exposure summary: what was reviewed, what urgent exposure was found, what was changed, what remains and the recommended next steps. You keep it whether or not you continue. There is no automatic continuation to a protection tier.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="b4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What if you find something serious outside my concern?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Dr. Tabansky explains it and obtains your approval before addressing it. If the proposed work expands the scope or price, that is agreed with you first. Finding an urgent problem does not authorize unagreed work or charges.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="b5">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can you remove spyware or a malicious app?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Where it can be done safely within the agreed scope, yes. Urgent first aid during the first step can include removing a malicious app or profile, with your approval. Dr. Tabansky explains each material change before acting. Removing it does not prove who installed it or how.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="c" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="c-h">
      <h2 id="c-h" class="h2">Protection tiers.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="c1" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What does Personal Shield include?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Personal Shield costs {{ facts.prices.personalShield | ils }} for one person, with the first step included. Dr. Tabansky hardens your phone, computer, accounts and home network around your risks, in person. It includes {{ facts.securityKeys.personalShield | numword }} security keys supplied, configured and tested, new core accounts and essential migration where needed, personal teaching, testing of material changes, a private dated record, a follow-up visit after about four weeks, and questions answered by WhatsApp or Signal for {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="c2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What do Personal Shield for Two and Inner Circle include?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Personal Shield for Two ({{ facts.prices.shieldForTwo | ils }}) is for you and one other person: each person's phone, computer and accounts, your home network and {{ facts.securityKeys.shieldForTwo | numword }} security keys. Inner Circle ({{ facts.prices.innerCircle | ils }}) is for a household of up to four, with {{ facts.securityKeys.innerCircle | numword }} security keys and a review visit at twelve months. Both include the follow-up visit and {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days of answered questions. If you authorize it, Dr. Tabansky coordinates with your lawyer or family office.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="c3">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>In Personal Shield for Two or Inner Circle, who sees whose records?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Each person receives a private dated record. The home-network work is recorded separately. Personal details are shared only with that person's consent; being part of the same engagement does not grant access to another person's information.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="c4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Does migration include all my files and old accounts?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Essential migration covers identity, recovery routes and critical-service access where needed. Historical archives and bulk data migration require a separately agreed scope. The written offer identifies the work to be done; the service does not promise unlimited accounts or data transfers.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="c5">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What does the {{ facts.questionLineDays }}-day question line cover?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>For {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days from completion of the tier's work, you can send questions by WhatsApp or Signal and receive an answer within one working day. It covers questions and guidance about your setup. It is not new work and not an emergency line; urgent needs go through an urgent visit. There is no remote control of your devices.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="d" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="d-h">
      <h2 id="d-h" class="h2">Privacy and control.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="d1">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Do I give you my passwords or remote access?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>You control your passwords, recovery codes and authentication throughout. Do not send them in advance. You may need to sign in on your own devices while we work. Toza does not keep your credentials for ongoing use or remotely control your devices.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="d2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Will you see my messages or photos?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Some information may be visible on your own screen where it is necessary for the agreed work, with you present. We explain the relevant access and agree what needs to be reviewed. The service is not a general inspection of your private content.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="d3">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Do you keep records or use the cloud?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Your situation and the information you share are handled confidentially. Your accounts and shared services may themselves use cloud systems. During the core engagement, Toza does not upload a client dataset to a Toza cloud-analysis platform or retain a copy or comprehensive log of your digital life beyond agreed deliverables and ordinary lawful business records. This does not mean that no cloud services or administrative records exist.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="d4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Do you monitor my devices or install software?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. Toza does not monitor your devices or install security software on them. The work focuses on the settings and access arrangements within your authorized environment. Every protection tier also includes practical security habits and personal teaching so you understand how to use the resulting setup.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="e" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="e-h">
      <h2 id="e-h" class="h2">What Toza does not do.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="e1">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can you prove who accessed my account, investigate someone or collect evidence?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. We examine your own authorized digital environment and reduce the exposure identified within the agreed scope. We do not investigate another person, attribute past activity, reconstruct events forensically, collect court evidence or give legal advice. Finding a current access path does not prove who used it or how information reached someone else. Changing access cannot recall copies already held elsewhere.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="e2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Will the other side notice the changes?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Some changes are visible. Ending a signed-in session, for example, signs that device out, and some changes create notifications for other users. We explain material changes and agree their timing and sequence with you before acting. We do not promise that changes will go unnoticed.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="e3">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Will this escalate my dispute? Is it legal?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Dr. Tabansky works only within your own authorized digital environment, on access you are authorized to manage. Changing recovery details or ending shared access can interrupt access or create notifications, so the effects are explained before you approve them. With your permission, timing can be coordinated with your attorney. Legal strategy stays with your attorney; Toza does not give legal advice.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="e4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can you work on company systems or a relative's account?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Only where you have lawful access and agreed authority. A dispute does not itself authorize changes to company systems or another person's accounts. A family connection does not authorize work on someone else's account or device. Toza does not determine who is entitled to an account, document or asset, and is not a corporate security audit.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="e5">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Is the dated record a certification or a security guarantee?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. It is a practical, dated account of the work performed, not a forensic report, legal opinion, court-evidence document or certification. A technically blocked or declined action is not presented as a completed change. The record does not guarantee that every possible exposure has been found or removed.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="e6">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>How is this different from IT support or a private investigator?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Other help is useful for its own scope:</p>
          <table class="faq-table mt-4">
            <caption class="sr-only">Other kinds of help and what each is useful for</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Useful for</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">IT support</th><td>Device faults, setup, maintenance and agreed technical work</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Apple, Google or Microsoft support</th><td>Questions within that provider's products</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">A password manager or antivirus</th><td>Managing credentials; detecting threats the product covers</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">A private investigator</th><td>Investigative work within an agreed lawful scope</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="mt-4">Toza applies expert judgment to your actual setup: tracing relevant connections, explaining what they allow and selecting changes in a considered sequence.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="f" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="f-h">
      <h2 id="f-h" class="h2">For attorneys.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="f1">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Does a referral authorize access to my client's information?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>No. A referral does not authorize access to devices, accounts or findings. The client must authorize the work and have lawful authority over the environment being reviewed. Coordination with counsel requires the client's permission; the referring attorney is not automatically a recipient of personal information or findings.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="f2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What does the attorney-friendly summary contain, and who decides?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>With the client's explicit authorization, an attorney-friendly summary can describe the work and remaining issues. The client decides what may be disclosed. It is a practical account of the work, not legal advice or a forensic report, and it does not establish what another person did.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="f3">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can timing be coordinated with proceedings?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Yes, with the client's permission. Timing of changes can be coordinated with counsel around a filing, a negotiation or a hearing. Legal strategy remains with the attorney; the client authorizes technical changes.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="f4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>How does referral work commercially?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>A referral fee is paid when a referred client's first step is paid, and a further fee if the client continues to a protection tier. Amounts and terms are in a one-page agreement.</p>
          <p class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ contact.referral.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t.buttons.referral }}</a></p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="g" class="faq-group" aria-labelledby="g-h">
      <h2 id="g-h" class="h2">Prices and timing.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 border-b border-rule">
      <details class="faq" id="g1" open>
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>How does the {{ facts.prices.assessment | ils }} first step count toward a tier?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>In full, when the tier's work begins within {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days of completion of the first step. You then pay the balance: {{ facts.prices.balanceShield | ils }} for Personal Shield, {{ facts.prices.balanceTwo | ils }} for Personal Shield for Two or {{ facts.prices.balanceInnerCircle | ils }} for Inner Circle. After day {{ facts.credit.windowDays }}, the tier is charged at its full price. If the first step shows you need the next tier, you pay that tier's price less the {{ facts.prices.assessment | ils }} already paid, within the same {{ facts.credit.windowDays }} days.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="g2">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What if the first step shows I need more than a tier includes?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Dr. Tabansky proposes the next tier, with its full allowance, before any work begins. Larger households, several residences or household staff receive one fixed price in writing after the first step, from {{ facts.prices.largerFrom | ils }}. There are no per-device or per-hour charges.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="g3">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>Can you come urgently, and what does it cost?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Availability is confirmed before you pay. For an accepted urgent booking, arrival is within four hours of both Toza's acceptance and receipt of payment. This is an arrival commitment, not a four-hour completion promise. The surcharge is {{ facts.prices.urgentSurcharge | ils }}, added to the agreed service price; at weekends or holidays it is {{ facts.prices.urgentSurchargeWeekend | ils }} instead.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" id="g4">
        <summary class="faq-q"><span>What happens after the {{ facts.questionLineDays }} days?</span><span class="faq-i" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a">
          <p>Past clients can continue with Annual Care: the question line on the same terms for twelve months, a check visit, setup of a new or replaced phone or computer, a replacement security key and an update to the dated record. It costs {{ facts.prices.annualCareOne | ils }} a year for one person, {{ facts.prices.annualCareTwo | ils }} for two and {{ facts.prices.annualCareHousehold | ils }} for a household of up to four. Join within {{ facts.annualCare.joinWindowMonths | numword }} months of the question line ending.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8"><a class="link font-semibold" href="/en/conditions/">All terms: Conditions <span class="flip" aria-hidden="true">{{ t.ui.arrow }}</span></a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
(function () {
  var b = document.getElementById("faq-toggle");
  if (!b) return;
  var all = function () { return document.querySelectorAll("details.faq"); };
  var sync = function () {
    var every = Array.prototype.every.call(all(), function (d) { return d.open; });
    b.textContent = every ? b.dataset.open : b.dataset.closed;
    b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", every ? "true" : "false");
  };
  b.hidden = false;
  b.addEventListener("click", function () {
    var every = Array.prototype.every.call(all(), function (d) { return d.open; });
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(all(), function (d) { d.open = !every; });
    sync();
  });
  Array.prototype.forEach.call(all(), function (d) { d.addEventListener("toggle", sync); });
  var h = location.hash && document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));
  if (h && h.tagName === "DETAILS") h.open = true;
  sync();
})();
</script>

